---
/**
 * `Ložnice a pokoje` + `Sociální zařízení`   the first section of /ubytovani.
 *
 * COPY IS THE OLD SITE'S, VERBATIM. This rebuild changes the design, not the
 * words. The two paragraphs below are the 2019 `/ubytovani/` page's own, with
 * `koupena` → `koupelna` fixed twice (docs/01-content.md §1 error #8) and
 * nothing else touched.
 *
 * DESIGN: the full-bleed split from the homepage   photograph running to one
 * viewport edge, prose holding its measure on the other. `.split` /
 * `.split--media-right` / `.split-media` / `.split-body` are the primitives in
 * global.css and this section adds no layout of its own beyond the bathroom
 * cards. Compare src/components/sections/Wellness.astro, which is the same
 * move mirrored. Alternating sides down the page is the point of it
 * (docs/02-design-system.md §3)   this one is media-right, so the next section
 * is media-left.
 *
 * The photograph is the living room, because the first sentence of the copy is
 * about the living room. That is the whole rule for picture choice on this page.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * ⚠ TWO CONTRADICTIONS ARE REPRODUCED HERE ON PURPOSE. DO NOT SILENTLY FIX.
 *
 * 1. **The capacities do not add up to 15.** These paragraphs give 2+1, then
 *    3–4 plus 2, then 6–8 plus 2   up to nineteen people, against the `2 až 15
 *    osob` printed at the top of this very page and everywhere else on the
 *    site. docs/01-content.md §9 item 1, launch-blocking, still unanswered.
 *
 *    An earlier pass "solved" this by replacing the prose with a tidy table
 *    reading 2 / 2+3 / 6+2 = 15, taken from the site-plan graphic. That is not
 *    a design decision, it is picking a winner in a factual dispute nobody has
 *    settled   so it is gone, and the client's own sentences are back. The
 *    contradiction is the client's to resolve; our job is not to hide it.
 *
 * 2. `1. NP` / `2. NP` here versus `první patro` / `druhé patro` in the
 *    bathroom paragraph, for the same two floors (§5.4). The prose is left
 *    alone; only the two CARD LABELS below were brought onto the `NP` scheme,
 *    so a reader is not asked to work out that `2. NP` and `druhé patro` are
 *    the same place. That is a label, which is design.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import obyvak from '@img/DSC_4579-scaled-1-1.jpg';
import SprigDivider from '../../decor/SprigDivider.astro';
import { SOCIALNI_ZARIZENI } from '../../../data/vybaveni';
---

<section id="loznice" class="loznice" aria-labelledby="loznice-nadpis">
  <div class="split split--media-right">
    <div class="split-media">
      <Image
        src={obyvak}
        alt="Obývací pokoj chalupy Heřmanka s krbem a dlouhým jídelním stolem pod dřevěným trámovým stropem, propojený s kuchyní"
        widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
        sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 50vw, 100vw"
        width={1920}
        height={1282}
        format="webp"
        quality={62}
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="split-body">
      <div data-reveal="up">
        <h2 id="loznice-nadpis">Ložnice a&nbsp;pokoje</h2>
        <p>
          V&nbsp;1.&nbsp;NP se nachází prostorný obývací pokoj s&nbsp;krbem spojený
          dohromady s&nbsp;prostornou kuchyní. Dále je zde menší pokoj (sousedící
          přímo s&nbsp;krytou terasou) s&nbsp;kapacitou 2&nbsp;dospělé osoby
          s&nbsp;dítětem. V&nbsp;přízemí se nachází samostatné WC a&nbsp;koupelna
          se sprchovým koutem.
        </p>
        <p>
          2.&nbsp;NP obsahuje jednu menší mezonetovou ložnici s&nbsp;kapacitou
          3&nbsp;až 4&nbsp;osoby dole a&nbsp;2&nbsp;osoby v&nbsp;horním patře. Tato
          ložnice má vstup na venkovní nekrytou terasu. Dále je zde větší
          mezonetová ložnice s&nbsp;kapacitou 6&nbsp;až 8&nbsp;osob dole
          a&nbsp;2&nbsp;osoby v&nbsp;horním patře. V&nbsp;tomto patře se nachází
          i&nbsp;koupelna s&nbsp;prostornou vanou, samostatné WC a&nbsp;prací
          a&nbsp;sušicí kout.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/*
    The bathrooms sit under the split rather than inside it. They are a
    comparison   the same three things on two floors   and a comparison wants
    two columns side by side, not a sentence that makes the reader hold one
    floor in their head while they read the other.
  */}
  <div class="wrap zarizeni">
    {/*
      Bilberry, not chamomile, and the two are alternated deliberately down the
      page so the ornament reads as a pair of local plants rather than as one
      motif stamped twice. BoruvkaSprig was drawn for the hero, lost its place
      when the hero was stripped back, and had been sitting unused since.
    */}
    <SprigDivider rostlina="boruvka" class="zarizeni-divider" />

    <h3 id="zarizeni-nadpis" data-reveal="up">Sociální zařízení</h3>

    <ul class="zarizeni-grid" role="list" data-reveal="up" data-reveal-delay="80">
      {
        SOCIALNI_ZARIZENI.map((z, i) => (
          <li class="card zarizeni-karta">
            <p class="zarizeni-patro">{i === 0 ? '1. NP' : '2. NP'}</p>
            <ul role="list">
              {z.polozky.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .loznice {
    background-color: var(--color-omitka);
  }

  h2 {
    /* --mosaz-tmava on --omitka = 6.05:1. Plain --mosaz as text would be a
       fill used as type, which §1.2 forbids. */
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }

  /*
   * `p` carries no margin at all in global.css   the reset is deliberate and
   * every component supplies its own rhythm. So this is not a tweak: without
   * it the first paragraph sits directly on the baseline of the heading.
   */
  .split-body p {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* ---- Bathrooms ------------------------------------------------------- */

  /*
   * The top padding is load-bearing. The split above runs its photograph to the
   * full height of its row and the picture's bottom edge is the section's own
   * edge, so without this the `Sociální zařízení` heading starts hard against
   * it and reads as a caption on the photograph rather than as a new heading.
   */
  .zarizeni {
    padding-block: 3rem 4rem;
  }

  @media (width >= 48rem) {
    .zarizeni {
      padding-block: 4.5rem 6rem;
    }
  }

  /* The divider does the separating now, so the heading sits closer under it
     than it did under bare padding. */
  .zarizeni-divider {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-title-m);
    color: var(--color-les);
  }

  .zarizeni-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    /* The measure rule still applies: two cards of short lines do not need the
       full 1280, and at full width the pair reads as two distant columns. */
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  @media (width >= 40rem) {
    .zarizeni-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
  }

  .zarizeni-patro {
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }

  .zarizeni-karta ul {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .zarizeni-karta li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  /* An en dash, not a disc: the same marker the old site used for its lists. */
  .zarizeni-karta li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-kura);
  }

  .zarizeni-karta li::before {
    content: '–';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    /* Brass AS TEXT, so the darker step (§1.2). */
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }
</style>
